speechtext:
1.	(a) Yes. "Crown and Commonwealth," was a reprint of an address on the coronation, and the imperial conference, delivered over the national network of the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation, on July 18th. 1937; (b) Yes.
2.	Cost of printing "Crown and Commonwealth", S228.81; cost of printing "The Struggle for Enduring Peace," $100.14.
3.	(a) Yes, by the Secretary of State for External Affairs; (b) Yes; (c) No.
4.	22,760 copies cost S328.95, as follows: "Crown and Commonwealth," 1,000 English, $52.38; External Affairs, 500 French, $59.71. Total, $112.09.
Public Printing and Stationery, 150 copies, $1.72; National Liberal Federation (reprints), 10,000 copies, $115. Total, $228.81.
"The Struggle for Enduring Peace"-External Affairs, 1,000 copies and envelopes, $29.52;
Public Printing and Stationery, 110 copies, 62 cents; National Liberal Federation (reprints), 10,000 copies, $70. Total, $100.14.
Grand total, $328.95.
5.	The following addresses delivered by the Prime Minister and Secretary of State for External Affairs outside the House of Commons other than those above mentioned were printed by the King's Printer;
On the occasion of the unveiling of the memorial at Vimy, July 26th, 1936, and on the occasion of the visit of President Roosevelt to Quebec, July 31st, 1936;
At the 17th session of the assembly of the League of Nations, Geneva, September 29th, 1936; being a statement of League of Nations policies;
On the occasion of the Canadian Legion Remembrance Day Broadcast, November 11th, 1936;
On the occasion of the visit to Canada of the Honourable Cordell Hull, Secretary of State of the United States, October 22nd, 1937;
At the dedication of The Thousand Islands International bridge at Ivy Lea, Ontario, and Collins Landing, N.Y., at the time of the visit to Canada of the President of the United States, on August 18th, 1938;
On the occasion of the Canadian Legion Remembrance Day broadcast, November 11th, 1938.
